{
  "dom_id": "step-q163646",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14130823/assets/c46bf82e7609abe56e9e65ef0e81e21438a67e849d80d560baff5ab0c90bde11.png)\n\nA plate with mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the curves $y={x}^{2}$ and $y=x+2$, as shown above. Given that the region has an area of $\\frac{9}{2},$ find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=2.$",
  "worked_solution": "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le x+2\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14130823/assets/f48cd4e22c083d6c05ba9908a788402b05d839fea710a7328297d9e392e3636e.png)\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-2|.\n$$\n\nSince the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{2M}{9}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{x+2}|x-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{x+2}(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(x-2)^{2}[y]_{y={x}^{2}}^{y=x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}({x}^{2}-4x+4)(x+2-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}-{x}^{4}+5{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-4x+8\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{[-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+\\frac{5{x}^{4}}{4}-2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+8x]}_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}[(-\\frac{32}{5}+20-16-8+16)-(\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{5}{4}+2-2-8)] \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}(\\frac{28}{5}-(-\\frac{131}{20})) \\\\  & =\\frac{27M}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
